from lesson_writer import author,CPP

def evidence(stem,oracle,detail,counts):
 def f(l):return 'The '+l(CPP/('support/'+oracle+'.java'),'Java oracle')+', '+l(CPP/('support/'+stem+'.cpp'),'native harness')+' and '+l(CPP/('tools/'+stem+'_differential.py'),'driver')+' '+detail+' The inspected '+l(CPP/('build/'+stem.replace('_','-')+'-results.json'),'report')+' records '+counts+' with zero failures. JDBC is recorded rather than executed by a native H2 engine. Clock arithmetic is validated before normalization; NPE expression text and logger prefixes/stacks are excluded.'
 return f
author('src/org/minima/database/txpowdb/onchain/TxPoWOnChainDB.md','Indexes the block in which a TxPoW became permanently on-chain, storing identifiers, height and insertion time.',[
 'Create an auto-increment table and prepare insertion, transaction lookup, block-ID/height lookup, earliest/latest timestamp, count and cleanup statements. The schema does not make txpowid unique; INSERT IGNORE alone therefore does not establish identifier deduplication.',
 'The default retention expression multiplies Java int literals before widening to long. Its stored value is 500,654,080 milliseconds, not the apparent thousand-day mathematical product. A faithful translation must reproduce that evaluated value.',
 'Insertion clears parameters, binds block ID, MiniNumber narrowed to long, TxPoW ID and current time in order. SQL failures are logged and return false; runtime failures escape.',
 'A transaction lookup initially returns found:false with the requested ID. It changes found to true before reading other fields, so a later SQL failure can return a partially populated found:true object.',
 'Block lookups append only fully decoded row objects. Earliest/latest reads add a date string; their ordering is by insertion timestamp, not block height.',
 'Cleanup deletes timestamps strictly below now minus retention. Hard mode calls the clock a second time and substitutes now plus 100,000. Wipe drops all objects and recreates the table, but does not rebuild prepared statements in this method.'
], 'C++ retains SQL text/call order through SqlDB services, uses atomic retention storage, Java-compatible signed wrap arithmetic and the existing date renderer. Shared prepared-statement references allow helper methods to observe replacements during reopen. This remains a storage-boundary implementation.',
 evidence('onchain_db','OnChainDBOracle','exercise all query overloads, null/partial rows, count narrowing, checked versus runtime failures at early JDBC calls, wipe/recreate, retention extremes, two clock calls in hard cleanup and seeded sequences.','855 programs, 3,639 operations and 29,167 driver calls'),
 'A row is found, but getLong(block) fails after found and blockid were written. What JSON survives? Why must the test compare the entire object rather than only found?',
 'Actual H2 execution, duplicate-row behavior under a real engine, durable files and full runtime integration remain absent. UTC fixture date comparisons do not establish every process timezone. Partial counterpart; parity not_verified.')
author('src/org/minima/database/txpowdb/sql/TxPoWSqlDB.md','Stores complete serialized TxPoW objects and searchable metadata, with retention that preserves relevant transactions.',[
 'Create a table with unique txpowid and an index over txpowid/parentid. Prepare exact-ID, block-child, count, relevance, newest-page and cleanup queries. The retention value is initialized at first class use from the configured days.',
 'Before insertion, optional block/transaction logs can inspect the object and transaction JSON. Then open the connection, serialize the TxPoW and bind ID, flags, parent, current time, bytes and relevance. Serialization failure can be logged before later bindings encounter the missing result.',
 'Reading retrieves bytes and uses TxPoW.convertMiniDataVersion. Malformed input can become null; list queries retain those null entries. A SQL failure after earlier rows returns the completed prefix.',
 'Relevant and newest queries bind limit then offset and sort by descending insertion time. Latest-size uses strictly greater than the supplied timestamp. Count failures return -1; exists catches SQL errors silently and returns false.',
 'customSizeQuery lowercases the entire condition, removes semicolons, then removes update, delete and insert in separate single passes before appending it to SQL. These textual edits can alter literals and are not a SQL parser or a proof of safe query construction.',
 'Cleanup deletes only old rows with isrelevant=0. Even hard cleanup preserves relevant rows because it changes the timestamp threshold, not that predicate. It can call the clock twice and logs around the operation when enabled.',
 'wipe recreates the table after DROP ALL OBJECTS without rebuilding the fast index or prepared statements. closeAndReopen saves without compaction, clears the connection and reopens through SqlDB.'
], 'Native code reuses the real TxPoW codec, SqlDB service boundary and Java lowercase helper. Its token-removal helper deliberately scans each original input once so newly formed matches survive that pass. Function-local retention initialization models Java class loading, and unsigned arithmetic followed by bit conversion models signed Java wrap.',
 evidence('txpow_sql_db','TxPoWSqlDBOracle','compare schema and prepared-statement identities, pagination, filtering edge cases, null receivers, faults during calls, cleanup/reopen and every truncated prefix of four real TxPoW fixtures. Logging/serialization failure timing and a nonempty transaction are included.','2,592 programs, 8,729 operations and 86,333 driver calls'),
 'Why does hard cleanup differ from wipe for a relevant transaction? Trace the exact DELETE predicate, then design one fixture that distinguishes the two operations.',
 'Recorded SQL text is not durable storage. Native H2 execution, every real driver failure, concurrency and full runtime ownership remain incomplete; count/default results can hide caught errors. The counterpart remains partial and parity not_verified.')
